//! Issue #8079: Past in Flames grants nothing.
//!
//! Every instant and sorcery card in the caster's graveyard at resolution
//! gains Flashback(SelfManaCost) (CR 611.2c). Each one WITH a mana cost is
//! offered at its mana cost, exiled after a flashback cast (CR 702.34a), and
//! loses the grant at cleanup (CR 514.2). This change claims nothing about a
//! card with no mana cost, so every instant or sorcery that Past in Flames or
//! Backdraft Hellkite grants below carries an explicit mana cost.
//!
//! CR 611.2c: "If a continuous effect generated by the resolution of a spell
//! or ability modifies the characteristics or changes the controller of any
//! objects, the set of objects it affects is determined when that continuous
//! effect begins." CR 109.2a: "card" plus a zone name means a card in that
//! zone. The untargeted grant used to bind battlefield permanents only, so a
//! filter naming the graveyard bound nothing and the grant was dropped.
//!
//! Rulings (Past in Flames 2021-03-19, Backdraft Hellkite 2019-08-23):
//! "Past in Flames affects only cards in your graveyard at the time it
//! resolves. Instant and sorcery cards put into your graveyard later in the
//! turn won't gain flashback." / "A spell cast using flashback will always be
//! exiled afterward." / "If a card has multiple instances of flashback, you
//! may choose any of its flashback costs to pay." / "If a split card gains
//! flashback, you pay only the cost of the half you're casting." / "If you
//! cast an instant or sorcery with {X} in its mana cost this way, you still
//! choose the value of X as part of casting the spell and pay that cost." /
//! "If the spell has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those to
//! cast the spell with flashback." / "You must still follow any timing
//! restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type." /
//! "Once Backdraft Hellkite has attacked, its ability will resolve and grant
//! the appropriate cards flashback even if Backdraft Hellkite leaves the
//! battlefield."
//!
//! Verbatim Oracle text (MTGJSON AtomicCards 5.3.0+20261122) for every fixture
//! below; Fire // Ice is a real card from the integration fixture.

